# A torch: a 12 V battery, a switch, and a 12 V 5 W lamp, with an ammeter in the lamp's lead.
#
# Click S1 to switch it on, and watch A1. Lit, the lamp draws its rated 5 W: 417 mA, through a
# filament of 28.8 Ω. But a tungsten filament's resistance rises tenfold as it heats, and it is cold
# when the switch closes: 2.9 Ω, which draws 4.2 A, ten times the steady current. As the filament
# heats the current falls away, to 1.7 A after 2 ms, under twice the steady current after 10 ms, and to
# within a percent of 417 mA after about 65 ms. This inrush is why a lamp most often fails at the
# moment it is switched on.
#
# The circuit runs at 20 ms a second, so the inrush takes three seconds to watch. Switch it off and the
# lamp's glow fades as its filament cools.

speed 20m

battery  B1   0 0  0 8  12V
switch   S1   0 0  6 0
ammeter  A1   6 0  12 0
lamp     L1   12 0  12 8  12V 5W
wire          0 8  12 8
ground        0 8
